      "index": "b0Q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1687201104,
      "version": 200,
      "versionNonce": 295911856,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794459988667,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Problem1: Never loose a click",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Problem1: Never loose a click",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "BWif-tmLoGE7hvypKZ9wJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 279.3837761335061,
      "y": 793.9753180992518,
      "width": 504.65692138671875,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 863696816,
      "version": 621,
      "versionNonce": 1496288176,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794459988667,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Solution: We can use fast & slow path pattern\n            Kafka will put click event data to object storage\n            Reconciliation service pull that data periodically & \n            recalculate expected count then compare it with saved\n            data in OLAP & update if there is any mismatch.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Solution: We can use fast & slow path pattern\n            Kafka will put click event data to object storage\n            Reconciliation service pull that data periodically & \n            recalculate expected count then compare it with saved\n            data in OLAP & update if there is any mismatch.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "BLQi4sZBfN9wIgHnvGKT1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 833.7933920033358,
      "y": 739.2792296822175,
      "width": 534.5595092773438,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0S",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1627962288,
      "version": 329,
      "versionNonce": 1287363408,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794459698572,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Problem2: Kafka goes down before receiving click event",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Problem2: Kafka goes down before receiving click event",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "T-yDGdtQRLz8HYpRVri4Y",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 830.465873474398,
      "y": 772.8578441183708,
      "width": 703.761474609375,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1372964272,
      "version": 1574,
      "versionNonce": 637465226,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "u-xJw_ChtGe1C8tcuvJ1d",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1794460220535,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Solution: If kafka goes down before receiving event, we can store that event in \n            a higly available queue (with backups & replicas). When kafka recovers,\n            those event will be published to kafka.\n\n            Why a queue and not in memory storage of click processor service.\n            There can be multiple instance of click processor running.\n            Click event for one ad can be stored in multiple instance's memory.\n            If any instance goes down, all stored data on that instance will be lost\n            Also even if we have backup, we have to coordinate multiple instances to collect\n            event for a ad.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Solution: If kafka goes down before receiving event, we can store that event in \n            a higly available queue (with backups & replicas). When kafka recovers,\n            those event will be published to kafka.\n\n            Why a queue and not in memory storage of click processor service.\n            There can be multiple instance of click processor running.\n            Click event for one ad can be stored in multiple instance's memory.\n            If any instance goes down, all stored data on that instance will be lost\n            Also even if we have backup, we have to coordinate multiple instances to collect\n            event for a ad.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
